Z||000000||BAM-BAM||10-16-2000||08:07 PM||||  Are the guages on an 85GT backlit or do they use offset lighting? I was thinking of getting some of those white face stickers but they say they will diminish a backlit guage. Otherwise I'll just stay with the standard black face.<P>  Thanks, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. If you like I can provide a link to the source. He-He-He-He, Oh, I kill me!!!<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-16-2000||08:29 PM||||Hey Bam Im not too sure about the 85's..however, I bought those sh1tty $15 white face guages of ebay and put them on my 87...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> my God, what was I thinking?<BR>After waiting almost a month for them to come in, I found that you had to cut out the hole for the needle and for the tripmeter...then, when I finally got them on, you could barely see them at night...<BR>They suck...now keep in mind, thats for those stickers ones that I got off ebay..others may be different. The only positive thing I can say about them is that they do look good in the daytime. <BR>I ended up taking them off.||||reg||13
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-16-2000||10:16 PM||||The '84-'85 Fieros use the offset lighting.  '86-'88 V-6 gauges are backlit.....I believe the '86-'88 coupes are offset too (not positive).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||10-17-2000||07:56 AM||||    That's the ones My7, But he did mention that the backlit guages had a problem at night and that it wouldn't effect the offset lit guages. I might just give it a try. I mean $15.00 wont kill me if it's a flop. Thanks for the info.<P> Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
